.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Rossler&#x27;s flow has a single nonlinear term, yet for a = b = 0.2, c = 5.7 it settles onto a chaotic attractor: orbits spiral outward near the plane z \approx 0, are lifted and folded back when x exceeds c, and never exactly repeat. Plotting each loop&#x27;s maximum of x against the previous one gives a Lorenz-style return map, a thin single-humped curve.">

