    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="For a stable linear system \dot x = Ax, solving the Lyapunov equation A^T P + PA = -Q gives an energy-like function V(x) = x^T P x whose level sets are ellipses that every trajectory crosses inward -- a proof of stability that never solves the ODE itself.">

